===Etymology===
{{ja-kanjitab|とら|yomi=k}}
{{swp|ja:トラ}}

From {{inh|ja|ojp|-|sort=とら}} ''to<sub>1</sub>ra'',<ref>{{R:jpx:ONCOJ|entry=twora|number=L090467}}</ref><ref>Thomas Pellard. [https://hal.archives-ouvertes.fr/hal-01289288/document Ryukyuan perspectives on the proto-Japonic vowel system]. Frellesvig, Bjarke; Sells, Peter. ''Japanese/Korean Linguistics'' 20, CSLI Publications, pp.81–96, 2013, 9781575866383. ffhal01289288</ref> from {{inh|ja|jpx-pro|*tora|sort=とら}}.

{{ja-ref|Pellard (2013, 92)}} includes ''to<sub>1</sub>ra'' among words with o<sub>1</sub> excepted from  the /-o-/ to /-u-/ vowel-raising rule and not originating from earlier diphthongs. According to {{ja-ref|Vovin (2021, 111)}}, West Old Japanese *''to<sub>1</sub>ra'', instead of expected *''tura'', is "anomalous" and possibly "a case of a sporadic analogical development".

{{ja-ref|Vovin (2013)}} asserts that this word is same as a Silla place name {{lang|oko|刀良}} ({{IPAfont|/*tora/}}), which matches the Old Japanese phonographic spelling.

